<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Muhammad Yunus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1940–</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Muhammad Yunus is a Bangladeshi economist who founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grameen-bank">Grameen Bank</a> and pioneered microcredit, lending small sums to the rural poor without collateral. He and the bank shared the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nobel-peace-prize">Nobel Peace Prize</a> in 2006. After mass protests forced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sheikh-hasina">Sheikh Hasina</a> from office in August 2024, he became chief adviser, the head of an interim government that organised elections in February 2026.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/muhammad-yunus.jpg" alt="Muhammad Yunus" width="320" height="441" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Press Information Department · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Muhammad_Yunus_speaking_at_Jamuna_State_Guesthouse,_Dhaka_2026-02-16_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
